---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import ModelSpecs from '../../components/brands/ModelSpecs.astro';
import { getModelSpecs } from '../../data/model-specs';

const models = getModelSpecs('Briggs & Stratton');
const toc = [
  { id: 'scope', label: 'Scope of this guide' },
  { id: 'model-data', label: 'PowerProtect 040786 data' },
  { id: 'warranty', label: 'Warranty and claims' },
  { id: 'quote-checklist', label: 'Quote checklist' },
];
---
<ArticleLayout
  title="Briggs & Stratton PowerProtect 040786: Verified Model Data"
  description="A source-linked guide to Briggs & Stratton PowerProtect standby generator model 040786, with separate LP/NG ratings, sound and fuel-use conditions, MSRP, warranty, and quote-scope caveats."
  category="Brands" categoryHref="/brands/" updated="2026-10-04" verified="2026-10-04" readingTime="6 min read" toc={toc}
  takeaways={[
    'Manufacturer data for model 040786 lists 22 kW on both LP and natural gas and a 45 kVA motor-starting capability.',
    'The product page lists a $6,037 starting MSRP and 7-year comprehensive limited warranty; neither is an installed quote or a substitute for full terms.',
    'The listed 68 dB(A) sound figure has no measurement distance stated on the product page.',
  ]}
  sources={[
    { label: 'Briggs & Stratton PowerProtect model 040786 product page and specifications', href: 'https://energy.briggsandstratton.com/en-us/products/powerprotect-22kw-standby-generator', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: '2026-10-04' },
    { label: 'Briggs & Stratton model 040786 specification sheet', href: 'https://briggs.widen.net/s/vxr2wjzrkp/16395_pp22_spec-sheet_10', type: 'Manufacturer', verified: '2026-10-04' },
  ]}
  related={[
    { href: '/brands/champion/', title: 'Champion 201222 model data', description: 'Ratings, included ATS, and separate warranty terms.', category: 'Brands' },
    { href: '/brands/generac/', title: 'Generac model data', description: 'Source-linked ratings, sound conditions, fuel use, and MSRP.', category: 'Brands' },
    { href: '/cost/standby-generator-cost/', title: 'Standby-generator cost guide', description: 'Compare manufacturer equipment prices with installed estimates.', category: 'Cost' },
  ]}
>
  <section id="scope">
    <h2>Scope of this guide</h2>
    <p>This page addresses exact Briggs & Stratton standby model <strong>040786</strong>, called PowerProtect 22 kW on the current product page. It does not summarize every PowerProtect capacity or imply independent reliability testing. Source data was checked October 4, 2026.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="model-data">
    <h2>PowerProtect 040786 manufacturer data</h2>
    <ModelSpecs models={models} label="Briggs & Stratton model 040786 specifications checked October 4, 2026" />
    <p class="mt-4">The manufacturer's 50%-load fuel-use values are reported in BTU/hr on its page. They are not gas volume rates; do not convert them into a household bill without fuel heating value, actual load, and local energy prices.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="warranty">
    <h2>Warranty summary and promotional claims</h2>
    <p>The manufacturer lists a <strong>7-year comprehensive limited warranty</strong> for model 040786 and says labor, parts, and service are included. Read the linked warranty document for the exact coverage conditions, required registration, start date, exclusions, and any limits that apply to the purchased model and installation.</p>
    <p>Briggs & Stratton markets the engine and warranty with comparative language such as “most comprehensive.” Those are manufacturer marketing claims; this publication has not independently ranked warranty coverage, motor-start performance, reliability, or service availability.</p>
  </section>

  <section id="quote-checklist">
    <h2>Before comparing a quote</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Confirm model number 040786 and its fuel-specific rating on the proposal.</li>
      <li>Ask whether a transfer switch is included; the cited generator product page does not establish an included switch package.</li>
      <li>Match motor-starting claims to actual equipment, system voltage, and load conditions.</li>
      <li>Ask for the warranty document and identify the local installer/service provider.</li>
      <li>Compare permits, fuel/electrical runs, pad/site work, inspections, startup, and exclusions line by line.</li>
    </ul>
    <p>See the <a href="/cost/standby-generator-cost/">standby cost guide</a> for how unit MSRP and installed-project estimates differ.</p>
  </section>
</ArticleLayout>
